WEBVTT

00:00:03.356 --> 00:00:08.793
♪ Hey, yeah... ♪

00:00:08.928 --> 00:00:11.367
(chuckles) You said that
it was for smoothies.

00:00:11.502 --> 00:00:13.533
It's called lying, Crimp.
Deal with me.

00:00:13.668 --> 00:00:14.964
If you use too much,
you'll kill him.

00:00:15.099 --> 00:00:17.802
The plum that I tested
turned into a prune!

00:00:17.937 --> 00:00:19.707
I don't want to kill
the little guy.

00:00:19.843 --> 00:00:21.707
They're kind of cute
when they're up and about,

00:00:21.842 --> 00:00:23.742
banging on the walls,
yelling to go home.

00:00:23.877 --> 00:00:25.776
Do you want to lose all this
and go back

00:00:25.911 --> 00:00:28.483
to the dark place
where we had nothing?

00:00:28.619 --> 00:00:31.246
(British accent):
Please, sir, I want some more.

00:00:31.382 --> 00:00:33.750
Girl, we grew up in the suburbs.
Our parents were dentists.

00:00:33.885 --> 00:00:36.320
PARENT:
So, how was school today?

00:00:36.455 --> 00:00:39.429
Stop attacking me!

00:00:39.564 --> 00:00:41.825
Our parents were nobodies,
and we were nobodies.

00:00:41.961 --> 00:00:43.763
And when I met you,
you were literally

00:00:43.899 --> 00:00:46.631
sucking your thumb
and pooping all over the place.

00:00:46.766 --> 00:00:48.532
You met me
when I was a baby, so...

00:00:48.667 --> 00:00:50.639
All over the place. It was nuts!

00:00:50.775 --> 00:00:52.968
You don't want to give up
all the yachts and the bling

00:00:53.103 --> 00:00:55.172
and your illegal pet monkey,
do you?

00:00:55.307 --> 00:00:57.880
(chuckles nervously) Okay.
I've made my peace with it.

00:00:58.015 --> 00:00:59.181
Great job, Cringe.

00:00:59.316 --> 00:01:01.115
You're smarter than I thought.

00:01:01.251 --> 00:01:02.483
Now I don't trust you.

00:01:02.619 --> 00:01:04.181
That's maybe not
a rational response.

00:01:04.316 --> 00:01:05.414
I don't, um... Please don't
put me in the closet.

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:06.951
Now, come on.

00:01:07.086 --> 00:01:09.826
We're about to go from stars
to megastars.

00:01:09.961 --> 00:01:11.027
Please, Veneer.

00:01:11.162 --> 00:01:12.427
It's nothing personal.

00:01:12.563 --> 00:01:15.224
I just love my sister
and all my fame

00:01:15.359 --> 00:01:18.197
- and money and things I bought.
- (elephant trumpets)

00:01:18.333 --> 00:01:19.766
Yeah, sure, dying sucks,

00:01:19.902 --> 00:01:21.369
but at least it's for
some sweet bling-a-ding

00:01:21.505 --> 00:01:23.667
and some boho-chic
home furnishings.

00:01:23.802 --> 00:01:25.336
(chuckling):
You get it.

00:01:25.472 --> 00:01:27.137
(Floyd groans, whimpers)

00:01:27.273 --> 00:01:28.675
Ow! Ooh!

00:01:30.341 --> 00:01:34.010
CRIMP: My Wi-Fi doesn't
work great in the closet.

00:01:34.146 --> 00:01:35.882
VELVET (over radio):
♪ Never gets old ♪

00:01:36.018 --> 00:01:38.817
♪ No matter how much I'm told
I'm amazing ♪

00:01:38.952 --> 00:01:40.122
VENEER:
♪ You're amazing... ♪

00:01:40.257 --> 00:01:41.619
Oh, my kids love these guys.

00:01:41.755 --> 00:01:43.456
We're a total Veneer household.

00:01:43.591 --> 00:01:45.358
They're the ones who have Floyd.

00:01:45.493 --> 00:01:46.625
Ah. It's gonna be hard

00:01:46.761 --> 00:01:48.157
to separate the art
from the artist.

00:01:48.292 --> 00:01:49.628
DJ (over radio):
That's Velvet and Veneer's

00:01:49.764 --> 00:01:51.399
spicy-hot new single
"Watch Me Work."

00:01:51.535 --> 00:01:52.963
Catch them tomorrow night
at the Rage Dome

00:01:53.099 --> 00:01:56.205
where they'll be receiving
the Lifer Award.

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:57.738
(distorted):
Lifer Award!

00:01:57.873 --> 00:01:59.475
Guys, will Floyd even make it
through that show?

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:01.005
Don't worry.
We're gonna make it.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:03.542
We've been looking for clues
to find Clay.

00:02:03.677 --> 00:02:05.509
Oh, I'm sorry. The clue board?

00:02:05.645 --> 00:02:07.476
You mean my clue board?

00:02:07.611 --> 00:02:09.486
That I made?

00:02:09.621 --> 00:02:12.417
- We like the clue board now?
- What is he wearing?

00:02:12.552 --> 00:02:13.651
Oh, those are just his...

00:02:13.787 --> 00:02:16.353
♪ Perfect, perfect, perfect. ♪

00:02:16.489 --> 00:02:19.462
...funderdrawers.

00:02:19.598 --> 00:02:21.728
- GHOSTS: Stinky.
- (Poppy and John Dory groaning)

00:02:21.863 --> 00:02:23.931
John Dory, I have no idea
why you saved these.

00:02:24.066 --> 00:02:27.467
It's incredibly disgusting,
but I'm glad you did.

00:02:27.602 --> 00:02:28.665
What? They're memorabilia.

00:02:28.801 --> 00:02:30.738
But I will be good gosh darned

00:02:30.874 --> 00:02:33.436
if I know how they're gonna
help us find Clay.

00:02:33.571 --> 00:02:34.844
♪ ♪

00:02:34.979 --> 00:02:36.274
(sniffing)

00:02:36.409 --> 00:02:37.409
Help us, Rhonda!

00:02:37.545 --> 00:02:39.612
She's got the scent.

00:02:39.748 --> 00:02:42.078
Oh, hey, Tiny.
You see that button?

00:02:43.987 --> 00:02:45.385
Uh, yeah.

00:02:45.521 --> 00:02:46.786
That beautiful, shiny button?

00:02:46.921 --> 00:02:48.523
Oh, you mean the button
that it's taking

00:02:48.659 --> 00:02:50.960
every fiber of my being
not to press?

00:02:51.095 --> 00:02:52.124
Yeah, I see it.

00:02:52.259 --> 00:02:53.929
Press it.

00:02:54.065 --> 00:02:56.461
Oh, heck yeah!

00:02:56.597 --> 00:02:58.934
Ooh! Let's hustle, daddy!

00:02:59.069 --> 00:03:01.471
♪ ♪

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:06.872
♪ Do it ♪

00:03:08.643 --> 00:03:09.571
- Whoa!
- ♪ Do it ♪

00:03:09.707 --> 00:03:12.542
Whoa. (gasps)

00:03:12.678 --> 00:03:14.477
♪ Do the hustle ♪

00:03:14.612 --> 00:03:16.546
♪ Yeah ♪

00:03:16.682 --> 00:03:17.848
♪ Do the hustle ♪

00:03:17.984 --> 00:03:19.789
♪ Every day I'm hustlin' ♪

00:03:19.924 --> 00:03:21.858
- ♪ Do the hustle ♪
- (echoing): ♪ Hustlin' ♪

00:03:21.993 --> 00:03:23.922
♪ Do it ♪

00:03:26.261 --> 00:03:29.026
♪ ♪

00:03:32.897 --> 00:03:34.299
(echoing):
Hustle!

00:03:34.434 --> 00:03:35.835
♪ Do it ♪

00:03:36.436 --> 00:03:37.903
♪ Do it ♪

00:03:38.571 --> 00:03:40.173
♪ Do it. ♪

00:03:40.308 --> 00:03:41.909
(all grunt)

00:03:42.045 --> 00:03:42.838
Wow.

00:03:42.973 --> 00:03:44.607
Too much hustle is a thing.

00:03:44.742 --> 00:03:47.147
Huh. Look at that.

00:03:47.282 --> 00:03:49.684
♪ ♪

00:03:55.022 --> 00:03:58.723
BRANCH: Are we sure
this is where Clay lives?

00:03:58.858 --> 00:04:00.289
TINY DIAMOND:
Are we sure?

00:04:00.425 --> 00:04:04.133
Our GPS is an armadillo bus
sniffing used undies,

00:04:04.269 --> 00:04:06.162
so no, we're not sure.

00:04:07.699 --> 00:04:08.933
(Spruce shudders)

00:04:09.069 --> 00:04:10.640
SPRUCE:
I think this is the place from

00:04:10.775 --> 00:04:13.070
every true crime podcast
I've ever listened to.

00:04:14.705 --> 00:04:17.008
♪ ♪

00:04:23.819 --> 00:04:27.122
BOOMING VOICE:
Halt! Who goes there?

00:04:27.257 --> 00:04:29.724
(all screaming)

00:04:31.256 --> 00:04:34.857
Who dares trespass
on these sacred grounds?

00:04:34.992 --> 00:04:37.195
Branch, what are you doing?

00:04:37.331 --> 00:04:42.870
Listen, we don't want
any clown-related trouble, okay?

00:04:43.006 --> 00:04:45.509
We're just here looking
for our brother Clay.

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:49.342
Wait a second.

00:04:49.477 --> 00:04:51.312
You're trolls?

00:04:51.448 --> 00:04:53.748
So what? You're a clown.

00:04:57.087 --> 00:04:58.621
Oh!

00:05:02.093 --> 00:05:03.486
Oh, my gosh.

00:05:03.621 --> 00:05:05.060
Hello!

00:05:05.195 --> 00:05:06.794
My name is Viva.

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:10.496
It is so fantastamazing
to see other trolls.

00:05:10.631 --> 00:05:12.068
(grunting, chuckling)

00:05:12.203 --> 00:05:13.703
- (grunts)
- Hi. Ha!

00:05:13.838 --> 00:05:16.704
So, "fantastamazing" is
my own personal word.

00:05:16.839 --> 00:05:18.740
It means, um,
fantastic and amazing.

00:05:18.875 --> 00:05:20.704
I used to say "amastic,"
but then I was like,

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:22.011
"Mm, that's not as good."

00:05:22.147 --> 00:05:23.876
Fantastamawesome!

00:05:24.012 --> 00:05:25.675
That's different,
but that works, too.

00:05:25.811 --> 00:05:27.111
Way to make it your own.

00:05:27.246 --> 00:05:28.813
Is this how people feel
when they meet me?

00:05:28.948 --> 00:05:30.318
- Yes.
- Am I being a lot?

00:05:30.453 --> 00:05:31.753
Sometimes I can be a lot.

00:05:31.888 --> 00:05:33.522
I'm not sure
we're in the right place.

00:05:33.657 --> 00:05:34.885
Course you're in
the right place.

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:36.518
Any troll is welcome here
with us.

00:05:36.654 --> 00:05:40.964
Okay, Putt Putt trolls,
lights on for our new friends.

00:05:41.099 --> 00:05:43.094
♪ ♪

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:47.637
- JOHN DORY: Wow.
- SPRUCE: Ooh.

00:05:47.772 --> 00:05:50.367
Oh, my gosh. Are you guys
hungry? Are you thirsty?

00:05:50.503 --> 00:05:51.672
Yes!

00:05:51.808 --> 00:05:52.768
Fries? Fries?
You guys want fries.

00:05:52.903 --> 00:05:54.004
I am seeing fries.

00:05:54.139 --> 00:05:56.112
- Bring out the works.
- Fries!

00:05:56.248 --> 00:05:58.242
Milkshakes to celebrate.

00:05:58.377 --> 00:06:01.145
- Coming in hot!
- TINY DIAMOND (laughing): Whoa!

